forti-mcp (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Engine: forti-cli v0.3.1 (d0e83a8), on forti-api 1.1.0's runtime schema: no
    typed shards; resource lookup by CLI words, unique last word and keyed
    path; attribute suggestions; profile lists and mode commands in error
    details; missing certificate files caught before any request.
  * Tool descriptions of forti_read / forti_discover name the new spellings.
  * Packaging: Homebrew bottle built and published with each release; build
    jobs budgeted at 1.2 GB; libforti-api-dev (>= 1.1.0).

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:58:07 +0000

forti-mcp (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Engine
    - The command engine is re-pinned to forti-cli 6a19035
      (subprojects/forti-cli.wrap and the Homebrew formula's forti-cli
      resource), the engine of forti-cli 0.2.0.
    - One forti home: `$FORTI_HOME`, else `~/.forti`, holds config.json,
      credentials/, state/, cache/ and certs/<profile>/. `FORTI_CONFIG_DIR`,
      `FORTI_STATE_DIR` and `FORTI_CACHE_DIR` still override single locations.
      A pre-0.2 setup (`~/.config/forti`, `~/.local/state/forti`,
      `~/.cache/forti` or the XDG variables) stays in use while the home has no
      config.json and neither `FORTI_HOME` nor `FORTI_CONFIG_DIR` is set;
      `forti home migrate` moves it.
    - Profiles can read a client certificate password from an owner-only file
      (secret source `file`), as written by `forti cert create`.
  * Tests and packaging
    - Tests build the engine's `Paths` with its new `home` member (no
      missing-field-initializers warning under GCC -Werror); the scripted
      transport gains `reply_raw`, in sync with forti-cli.
    - The e2e tests, the smoke test and the Homebrew formula test set a
      temporary `FORTI_HOME`, so they never resolve the real forti home.
  * Documentation
    - The docs are built around the forti home and the `~/.forti` workspace:
      + Connecting AI clients leads with `forti install mcp --scope workspace`
        (`cd ~/.forti && claude` or `codex`), why the tools stay out of other
        projects, Codex trust (`--trust-codex-workspace`), and the Claude Code
        deny rules and Codex `forti-workspace` permission profile; manual
        registration remains the alternative.
      + Installation documents the forti home, `forti home` and upgrading with
        `forti home migrate`; the command-line reference lists the home's
        locations and overrides.
      + Security covers where secrets and certificates live and the workspace
        deny rules.
      + New guide, Several FortiGates: a profile per device, `--profile` and
        the per-request `profile` field.

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:44:17 +0000

